+# Phase 5 Plan 01: Answer and groundedness contracts Summary
+
+**Pydantic v2 source of truth for CitationRecord, AnswerRecord, feedback and the sidecar groundedness wire, with generated Zod, samples and the default 0.5 thresholds file.**
+
+## Performance
+
+- **Tasks:** 2 (plus a RED commit for the TDD task)
+- **Files:** 10 created, 5 modified
+
+## Accomplishments
+
+- CitationRecord carries exactly the D-01 fields; alias pattern `^S[1-9][0-9]*$`, quoteHash `^[0-9a-f]{64}$`, strategy limited to claude-citations and chunk-alias, quote not capped (the app caps message metadata at 1,000 characters, D-03).
+- AnswerGroundedness, GroundednessResult and GroundednessThresholds enforce the per-status rules and (scorer, language) uniqueness through validators.
+- AnswerFeedbackRequest: vote enum, at most four unique reason chips, comment at most 500, optional UUID chatId.
+- `eval/config/groundedness-thresholds.json` holds three default 0.5 cells (hhem_2_3_vectara en and zh-Hans, hhem_2_1_open en); a test loads it through GroundednessThresholds.
+- Registered in CONTRACTS (validation for GroundednessRequest and AnswerFeedbackRequest, serialization for the other four) with one invented-text sample each.
+
